    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to help responders locate the turn-in under low visibility or nighttime conditions.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of parked vehicles so fire apparatus and ambulances can reach the residence without stopping.\n• Maintain driveway width and overhead clearance along the full length of the drive to allow large emergency vehicles to pass through without obstruction.\n• Identify and mark a turnaround area near the residence so apparatus are not required to back the full length of the driveway to exit.\n• Keep a secondary foot path or vehicle route along the rear of the property clear so responders can reach the back of the residence on foot if the driveway is blocked.\n• Trim any landscaping along the driveway edges that narrows the travel path or reduces sight lines for an approaching driver.\n• Post the physical address number visibly at the road and again near the residence so responders can confirm they have reached the correct structure."
