    "recommendations": "• Trim any shrubs growing directly against or within a few feet of the house walls.\n• Thin the tree cluster nearest to the structure to create more open space between individual trees.\n• Remove grass and low ground cover growing close to the base of the structure.\n• Keep shrubs scattered across the property trimmed low and separated from each other to reduce connected plant material across the open terrain.\n• Clear overhanging branches and shrubs along the full length of the driveway so vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is easy to find quickly, since there is only one way in and out.\n• Maintain the existing open areas between the scattered trees and the structure by preventing new shrub or grass growth from filling those gaps.\n• Remove any dead or dry grass that has accumulated near the structure or along the driveway edge.\n• Keep the area under the tree cluster clear of fallen branches, leaves, and dry debris that could carry fire toward the house."
